 "text": "The actual speedup depends on draft accuracy, verification cost, memory bandwidth, and hardware efficiency. If too many draft tokens get rejected, the extra work may outweigh the benefit. So the central idea is simple. MTP proposes future tokens. Speculative decoding verifies them. And when enough predictions are accepted, the model can generate text faster, without changing the target decoding result or distribution.",
